IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `vrsa-core`

-- Victims Rights and Support Act 2013 (NSW) and Victims Rights and Support Regulation 2019 -- tests of the core.
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited texts (act-2013-037.txt, sl-2019-0398.txt), with the
-- reasoning or arithmetic in the comment above the assertion. Records and calls are formatted from a table by the
-- scratchpad generator au-nsw-6/gen_vrsa_cases.py; no expected value was taken from the encoding's output.
-- Regulative rules: each fulfilled trace is asserted with EVALTRACE ... EQUALS FULFILLED; a breach or a pending
-- obligation is shown with #TRACE and an "-- expect:" line, read by hand. Clock: days.
-- Not the current official text; it may be out of date.

§ `Cases -- the core`

§§ `Dates`

-- 10 March 2023 + 2 years = 10 March 2025; 2024 is a leap year, so 366 + 365 = 731 days.
#ASSERT 2 `years after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 3 2023) EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 10 3 2025
#ASSERT `the days from` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 3 2023) `to` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 3 2025) EQUALS 731
-- 1 July 2023 to 1 July 2028 crosses 29 February 2024 and 29 February 2028: 5 x 365 + 2 = 1827.
#ASSERT `the days from` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2023) `to` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2028) EQUALS 1827
-- READING: 29 February 2024 + 2 years falls on 28 February 2026; + 4 years on 29 February 2028.
#ASSERT 2 `years after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 29 2 2024) EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 2026
#ASSERT 4 `years after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 29 2 2024) EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 29 2 2028
-- Born 15 June 2007: turns 18 on 15 June 2025; a child on 14 June 2025, not on 15 June 2025.
#ASSERT `was a child on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 6 2007) (DATE_FROM_DMY 14 6 2025)
#ASSERT NOT (`was a child on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 6 2007) (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 6 2025))

§§ `The acts and the people (records)`

-- s 19(1)(a)-(c) all met, in NSW
`act: an assault in a pub in Sydney` MEANS
    `The act` WITH
        `apparently occurred in the course of the commission of an offence`                             IS TRUE
        `involved violent conduct against one or more persons`                                          IS TRUE
        `resulted in injury or death to one or more of those persons`                                   IS TRUE
        `was committed in New South Wales`                                                              IS TRUE
        `apparently occurred in the course of an offence or other conduct constituting modern slavery`  IS FALSE
        `involved subjecting one or more persons to slavery, servitude or forced labour of a child`     IS FALSE
        `resulted in injury or death to one of the persons subjected to it`                             IS FALSE
        `involved a motor vehicle and caused the death of another person`                               IS FALSE
        `charges have been laid against the alleged offender`                                           IS FALSE
        `the alleged offender has died or cannot be identified, and an offence has apparently occurred` IS FALSE
        `took the form of, or the injury arose from, a motor accident`                                  IS FALSE
        `took the form of the intentional killing of the primary victim`                                IS FALSE
        `a person has been charged with murder in relation to the death`                                IS FALSE
        `was a terrorist act`                                                                           IS FALSE

