§§ `ss 19, 19A, 19AB, 30A -- what kind of act`

-- an offence, violent conduct, injury: s 19(1)
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `act: an assault in a pub in Sydney` EQUALS (LIST `an act of violence (s 19)`)
-- s 19(1)(a) not met
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `act: no offence apparently committed` EQUALS EMPTY
-- s 19(1)(c) not met
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `act: violence without injury` EQUALS EMPTY
-- both s 19 and s 19A; s 30A applies
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `act: forced labour with violence, in NSW` EQUALS (LIST `an act of violence (s 19)`, `an act of modern slavery (s 19A)`)
-- s 19A only
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `act: modern slavery without violent conduct, in NSW` EQUALS (LIST `an act of modern slavery (s 19A)`)
-- s 19A(1): "committed in New South Wales"
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `act: modern slavery outside NSW` EQUALS EMPTY
-- s 19 has no place requirement (finding 1)
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `act: an assault in Melbourne` EQUALS (LIST `an act of violence (s 19)`)
-- s 19AB(1)(a), (b)(i); s 19(3A): not an act of violence
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `act: a death by dangerous driving, driver charged` EQUALS (LIST `a road crime (s 19AB)`)
-- s 19(3A) with s 25(2A): both
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `act: a driver deliberately kills, charged with murder` EQUALS (LIST `an act of violence (s 19)`, `a road crime (s 19AB)`)
-- s 19AB(1)(b)(ii)
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `act: a fatal crash, driver died` EQUALS (LIST `a road crime (s 19AB)`)
-- no death: not a road crime; an act of violence
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `act: a deliberate car assault, injury only` EQUALS (LIST `an act of violence (s 19)`)
-- s 19(3A) with s 25(2B): both
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `act: a vehicle terrorist attack` EQUALS (LIST `an act of violence (s 19)`, `a road crime (s 19AB)`)
-- s 19AB(1)(b) not met: not a road crime, so s 19(3A) does not bite
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `act: a vehicle death, offender identified, not charged` EQUALS (LIST `an act of violence (s 19)`)
-- s 30A(1): an act that is 2 or more kinds.
#ASSERT `s 30A applies to` `act: forced labour with violence, in NSW`
#ASSERT `s 30A applies to` `act: a driver deliberately kills, charged with murder`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 30A applies to` `act: an assault in a pub in Sydney`)

§§ `ss 20 to 25 -- victims, eligibility and exclusions`

-- s 20(1)
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: an assault in a pub in Sydney` `person: injured` EQUALS (LIST (`eligible as` `a primary victim (s 23(1), s 26)`))
-- s 20(2)(b)
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: an assault in a pub in Sydney` `person: injured rescuing` EQUALS (LIST (`eligible as` `a primary victim (s 23(1), s 26)`))
-- s 21(1)
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: an assault in a pub in Sydney` `person: a witness, injured` EQUALS (LIST (`eligible as` `a secondary victim (s 23(3), s 28)`))
-- s 21(2)(a)-(c)
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: an assault in a pub in Sydney` `person: a parent who learnt of it later, child 15` EQUALS (LIST (`eligible as` `a secondary victim (s 23(3), s 28)`))
-- s 21(2)(b): the primary victim was not under 18
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: an assault in a pub in Sydney` `person: a parent who learnt of it later, child 19` EQUALS (LIST `not a victim of an act of violence, an act of modern slavery or a road crime (ss 19 to 23)`)
-- s 21(2)(c): the person committed the act
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: an assault in a pub in Sydney` `person: a parent who learnt of it later and committed it` EQUALS (LIST `not a victim of an act of violence, an act of modern slavery or a road crime (ss 19 to 23)`)
-- s 23(2)
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: an assault in a pub in Sydney` `person: a carer of the injured child` EQUALS (LIST (`eligible as` `a parent, step-parent or guardian caring for a child primary victim (s 23(2), s 27)`))
-- s 23(2) and s 21(1)
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: an assault in a pub in Sydney` `person: a carer who also witnessed it` EQUALS (LIST (`eligible as` `a parent, step-parent or guardian caring for a child primary victim (s 23(2), s 27)`), (`eligible as` `a secondary victim (s 23(3), s 28)`))
-- none of ss 20-23
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: an assault in a pub in Sydney` `person: not affected` EQUALS (LIST `not a victim of an act of violence, an act of modern slavery or a road crime (ss 19 to 23)`)
-- no act of violence (s 19(1)(a))
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: no offence apparently committed` `person: injured` EQUALS (LIST `not a victim of an act of violence, an act of modern slavery or a road crime (ss 19 to 23)`)
-- s 22(1), (3)(a)
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: a fatal stabbing` `person: spouse of the person who died` EQUALS (LIST (`eligible as` `a family victim of an act of violence (s 23(4), s 29)`))
-- s 22(3)(b): cohabited less than 2 years
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: a fatal stabbing` `person: de facto partner of 18 months` EQUALS (LIST `not a victim of an act of violence, an act of modern slavery or a road crime (ss 19 to 23)`)
-- s 22(3)(b)
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: a fatal stabbing` `person: de facto partner of 3 years` EQUALS (LIST (`eligible as` `a family victim of an act of violence (s 23(4), s 29)`))
-- s 22(3)(e)
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: a fatal stabbing` `person: sister of the person who died` EQUALS (LIST (`eligible as` `a family victim of an act of violence (s 23(4), s 29)`))
-- a cousin is not immediate family (s 22(3))
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: a fatal stabbing` `person: cousin of the person who died` EQUALS (LIST `not a victim of an act of violence, an act of modern slavery or a road crime (ss 19 to 23)`)
-- s 20(1) and s 22(1); s 22(2): injury immaterial
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: a fatal stabbing` `person: spouse, injured too` EQUALS (LIST (`eligible as` `a primary victim (s 23(1), s 26)`), (`eligible as` `a family victim of an act of violence (s 23(4), s 29)`))
-- s 25(1)
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: an assault in a pub in Sydney` `person: injured, with court compensation` EQUALS (LIST (`not eligible as` `a primary victim (s 23(1), s 26)` `compensation awarded by a court under Part 6 has been paid, is payable or has been applied for (s 25(1))`))
-- s 25(3)(a)
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: an assault in a pub in Sydney` `person: injured while committing an offence` EQUALS (LIST (`not eligible as` `a primary victim (s 23(1), s 26)` `the act occurred while the person was engaged in behaviour constituting an offence (s 25(3)(a))`))
-- s 25(4); the Commissioner has not found special circumstances
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: an assault in a pub in Sydney` `person: injured as a convicted inmate` EQUALS (LIST (`not eligible as` `a primary victim (s 23(1), s 26)` `a convicted inmate when the act occurred, unless the Commissioner is satisfied that special circumstances justify an exception (s 25(4), (5))`))
-- s 25(5)
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: an assault in a pub in Sydney` `person: injured as a convicted inmate, special circumstances` EQUALS (LIST (`eligible as` `a primary victim (s 23(1), s 26)`))
-- s 24(1)
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: an assault in a pub in Sydney` `person: injured, has since died` EQUALS (LIST (`not eligible as` `a primary victim (s 23(1), s 26)` `the victim has died: the victim ceases to be eligible, and a pending application does not survive (s 24)`))
-- s 25(3)(a) speaks only of an act of violence; the act is also an act of modern slavery (finding 5)
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: forced labour with violence, in NSW` `person: injured while committing an offence` EQUALS (LIST (`eligible as` `a primary victim (s 23(1), s 26)`))
-- s 25(3)(a) does not reach an act of modern slavery
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: modern slavery without violent conduct, in NSW` `person: injured while committing an offence` EQUALS (LIST (`eligible as` `a primary victim (s 23(1), s 26)`))
-- s 21: secondary victims only of an act of violence
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: modern slavery without violent conduct, in NSW` `person: a witness, injured` EQUALS (LIST `not a victim of an act of violence, an act of modern slavery or a road crime (ss 19 to 23)`)
-- s 22: family victims only of an act of violence or a road crime (finding 4)
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: modern slavery without violent conduct, in NSW` `person: spouse of the person who died` EQUALS (LIST `not a victim of an act of violence, an act of modern slavery or a road crime (ss 19 to 23)`)
-- s 25(2); no terrorist act
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: a deliberate car assault, injury only` `person: injured` EQUALS (LIST (`not eligible as` `a primary victim (s 23(1), s 26)` `the act took the form of, or the injury arose from, a motor accident (s 25(2))`))
-- s 25(2)
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: a deliberate car assault, injury only` `person: a witness, injured` EQUALS (LIST (`not eligible as` `a secondary victim (s 23(3), s 28)` `the act took the form of, or the injury arose from, a motor accident (s 25(2))`))
-- s 25(2B)
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: a vehicle terrorist attack` `person: injured` EQUALS (LIST (`eligible as` `a primary victim (s 23(1), s 26)`))
-- s 25(2B) names only primary and family victims (finding 6)
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: a vehicle terrorist attack` `person: a witness, injured` EQUALS (LIST (`not eligible as` `a secondary victim (s 23(3), s 28)` `the act took the form of, or the injury arose from, a motor accident (s 25(2))`))
-- s 25(2B), and s 22(1A)
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: a vehicle terrorist attack` `person: spouse of the person who died` EQUALS (LIST (`eligible as` `a family victim of an act of violence (s 23(4), s 29)`), (`eligible as` `a family victim of a road crime (s 23(5), s 29A)`))
-- s 22(1A), s 23(5)
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: a death by dangerous driving, driver charged` `person: spouse of the person who died` EQUALS (LIST (`eligible as` `a family victim of a road crime (s 23(5), s 29A)`))
-- not an act of violence (s 19(3A)), so no primary victim
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: a death by dangerous driving, driver charged` `person: injured` EQUALS (LIST `not a victim of an act of violence, an act of modern slavery or a road crime (ss 19 to 23)`)
-- s 25(2A) and s 22(1A)
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: a driver deliberately kills, charged with murder` `person: spouse of the person who died` EQUALS (LIST (`eligible as` `a family victim of an act of violence (s 23(4), s 29)`), (`eligible as` `a family victim of a road crime (s 23(5), s 29A)`))
-- s 25(2A) is for family victims only
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: a driver deliberately kills, charged with murder` `person: injured` EQUALS (LIST (`not eligible as` `a primary victim (s 23(1), s 26)` `the act took the form of, or the injury arose from, a motor accident (s 25(2))`))
-- s 25(2)
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: a driver deliberately kills, charged with murder` `person: a witness, injured` EQUALS (LIST (`not eligible as` `a secondary victim (s 23(3), s 28)` `the act took the form of, or the injury arose from, a motor accident (s 25(2))`))
-- s 25(3)(b)
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: a fatal crash, driver died` `person: spouse of the driver who died` EQUALS (LIST (`not eligible as` `a family victim of a road crime (s 23(5), s 29A)` `a family victim of the road crime only as a member of the alleged offender's immediate family (s 25(3)(b))`))
-- s 25(3A)
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: a fatal crash, driver died` `person: mother of the driver and of a passenger who died` EQUALS (LIST (`eligible as` `a family victim of a road crime (s 23(5), s 29A)`))
-- s 25(1) speaks only of an act of violence or act of modern slavery
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: a death by dangerous driving, driver charged` `person: spouse, with court compensation` EQUALS (LIST (`eligible as` `a family victim of a road crime (s 23(5), s 29A)`))
-- s 25(4) likewise
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: a death by dangerous driving, driver charged` `person: spouse, a convicted inmate` EQUALS (LIST (`eligible as` `a family victim of a road crime (s 23(5), s 29A)`))
-- s 25(4)
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: a fatal stabbing` `person: spouse, a convicted inmate` EQUALS (LIST (`not eligible as` `a family victim of an act of violence (s 23(4), s 29)` `a convicted inmate when the act occurred, unless the Commissioner is satisfied that special circumstances justify an exception (s 25(4), (5))`))
-- an act of violence that is a motor accident, and s 25(2A) needs a murder charge
#ASSERT `the victim statuses of` `act: a vehicle death, offender identified, not charged` `person: spouse of the person who died` EQUALS (LIST (`not eligible as` `a family victim of an act of violence (s 23(4), s 29)` `the act took the form of, or the injury arose from, a motor accident (s 25(2))`))

§§ `ss 26 to 30A -- the support, with the Regulation's maxima`

-- s 26(1)(a)-(d); cl 10(1) $5,000, cl 10(2) $30,000
#ASSERT `the support for` `act: an assault in a pub in Sydney` `person: injured` EQUALS (LIST `approved counselling services (ss 26(1)(a), 28, 29(1)(a), 29A)`, (`financial assistance for immediate needs (s 26(1)(b)), up to` 5000), (`financial assistance for economic loss (s 26(1)(c)), up to` 30000), `a recognition payment, if one is payable for the act (s 26(1)(d))`)
-- s 28: counselling only
#ASSERT `the support for` `act: an assault in a pub in Sydney` `person: a witness, injured` EQUALS (LIST `approved counselling services (ss 26(1)(a), 28, 29(1)(a), 29A)`)
-- s 27, cl 11(1) $30,000; no counselling (finding 7)
#ASSERT `the support for` `act: an assault in a pub in Sydney` `person: a carer of the injured child` EQUALS (LIST (`financial assistance for economic loss while caring for the child (s 27), up to` 30000))
-- s 27 and s 28
#ASSERT `the support for` `act: an assault in a pub in Sydney` `person: a carer who also witnessed it` EQUALS (LIST `approved counselling services (ss 26(1)(a), 28, 29(1)(a), 29A)`, (`financial assistance for economic loss while caring for the child (s 27), up to` 30000))
-- s 29(1)(a)-(d), (3); cl 12(1) $5,000, (2) $9,500, (3) $5,000
#ASSERT `the support for` `act: a fatal stabbing` `person: spouse of the person who died` EQUALS (LIST `approved counselling services (ss 26(1)(a), 28, 29(1)(a), 29A)`, (`financial assistance for immediate needs (s 29(1)(b)), up to` 5000), (`funeral expenses (s 29(1)(c)), up to this total for all the family victims` 9500), (`financial assistance for justice related expenses (s 29(1)(d)), up to` 5000), `a category A recognition payment, if one is payable to the person (s 29(3))`)
-- both s 26 and s 29; counselling once
#ASSERT `the support for` `act: a fatal stabbing` `person: spouse, injured too` EQUALS (LIST `approved counselling services (ss 26(1)(a), 28, 29(1)(a), 29A)`, (`financial assistance for immediate needs (s 26(1)(b)), up to` 5000), (`financial assistance for economic loss (s 26(1)(c)), up to` 30000), `a recognition payment, if one is payable for the act (s 26(1)(d))`, (`financial assistance for immediate needs (s 29(1)(b)), up to` 5000), (`funeral expenses (s 29(1)(c)), up to this total for all the family victims` 9500), (`financial assistance for justice related expenses (s 29(1)(d)), up to` 5000), `a category A recognition payment, if one is payable to the person (s 29(3))`)
-- s 29A: counselling only
#ASSERT `the support for` `act: a death by dangerous driving, driver charged` `person: spouse of the person who died` EQUALS (LIST `approved counselling services (ss 26(1)(a), 28, 29(1)(a), 29A)`)
-- s 29 and s 29A; s 30A: counselling once
#ASSERT `the support for` `act: a driver deliberately kills, charged with murder` `person: spouse of the person who died` EQUALS (LIST `approved counselling services (ss 26(1)(a), 28, 29(1)(a), 29A)`, (`financial assistance for immediate needs (s 29(1)(b)), up to` 5000), (`funeral expenses (s 29(1)(c)), up to this total for all the family victims` 9500), (`financial assistance for justice related expenses (s 29(1)(d)), up to` 5000), `a category A recognition payment, if one is payable to the person (s 29(3))`)
-- excluded by s 25(1)
#ASSERT `the support for` `act: an assault in a pub in Sydney` `person: injured, with court compensation` EQUALS EMPTY
-- not a victim
#ASSERT `the support for` `act: an assault in a pub in Sydney` `person: not affected` EQUALS EMPTY

§§ `s 26, s 30(2), Reg cl 10 -- a primary victim's financial assistance`

`claim: primary victim, earner, modest` MEANS
    `Primary victim claim` WITH
        `immediate needs expenses`                                           IS (`Expense` WITH `amount` IS 3200, `paid or payable from another source` IS 0)
        `can demonstrate actual loss of earnings`                            IS TRUE
        `weekly rate of actual loss of earnings under cl 9`                  IS 900
        `weeks of actual loss of earnings`                                   IS 12
        `lost earnings paid or payable from another source`                  IS 0
        `out-of-pocket expenses`                                             IS (`Expense` WITH `amount` IS 700, `paid or payable from another source` IS 0)
        `medical and dental expenses not claimed as immediate needs`         IS (`Expense` WITH `amount` IS 4000, `paid or payable from another source` IS 1500)
        `justice related expenses`                                           IS (`Expense` WITH `amount` IS 800, `paid or payable from another source` IS 0)
        `clothing and personal effects`                                      IS (`Expense` WITH `amount` IS 2000, `paid or payable from another source` IS 0)
        `paid or approved to the parent, step-parent or guardian under s 27` IS 0

-- immediate needs 3,200 (under $5,000); earnings 900 x 12 = 10,800 (under $20,000); out-of-pocket not assessed (earnings shown, cl 10(3)(b)); medical 4,000 - 1,500 Medicare = 2,500; justice 800; clothing 2,000 capped at 1,500; economic loss 10,800 + 2,500 + 800 + 1,500 = 15,600; total 3,200 + 15,600 = 18,800
#ASSERT (`the s 26 financial assistance for` `claim: primary victim, earner, modest`)'s `for immediate needs` EQUALS 3200
#ASSERT (`the s 26 financial assistance for` `claim: primary victim, earner, modest`)'s `for actual loss of earnings` EQUALS 10800
#ASSERT (`the s 26 financial assistance for` `claim: primary victim, earner, modest`)'s `for out-of-pocket expenses` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`the s 26 financial assistance for` `claim: primary victim, earner, modest`)'s `for medical and dental expenses` EQUALS 2500
#ASSERT (`the s 26 financial assistance for` `claim: primary victim, earner, modest`)'s `for justice related expenses` EQUALS 800
#ASSERT (`the s 26 financial assistance for` `claim: primary victim, earner, modest`)'s `for clothing and personal effects` EQUALS 1500
#ASSERT (`the s 26 financial assistance for` `claim: primary victim, earner, modest`)'s `for economic loss, within the maximum` EQUALS 15600
#ASSERT (`the s 26 financial assistance for` `claim: primary victim, earner, modest`)'s `taken off under s 26(2) or s 27(2)` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`the s 26 financial assistance for` `claim: primary victim, earner, modest`)'s `in total` EQUALS 18800

`claim: primary victim, every cap reached` MEANS
    `Primary victim claim` WITH
        `immediate needs expenses`                                           IS (`Expense` WITH `amount` IS 7000, `paid or payable from another source` IS 0)
        `can demonstrate actual loss of earnings`                            IS TRUE
        `weekly rate of actual loss of earnings under cl 9`                  IS 1500
        `weeks of actual loss of earnings`                                   IS 20
        `lost earnings paid or payable from another source`                  IS 4000
        `out-of-pocket expenses`                                             IS (`Expense` WITH `amount` IS 0, `paid or payable from another source` IS 0)
        `medical and dental expenses not claimed as immediate needs`         IS (`Expense` WITH `amount` IS 9000, `paid or payable from another source` IS 0)
        `justice related expenses`                                           IS (`Expense` WITH `amount` IS 6000, `paid or payable from another source` IS 0)
        `clothing and personal effects`                                      IS (`Expense` WITH `amount` IS 500, `paid or payable from another source` IS 0)
        `paid or approved to the parent, step-parent or guardian under s 27` IS 0

-- immediate needs 7,000 capped at 5,000; earnings 1,500 x 20 = 30,000 - 4,000 workers compensation = 26,000, capped at 20,000; medical 9,000; justice 6,000 capped at 5,000; clothing 500; 20,000 + 9,000 + 5,000 + 500 = 34,500, capped at 30,000; total 35,000
#ASSERT (`the s 26 financial assistance for` `claim: primary victim, every cap reached`)'s `for immediate needs` EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT (`the s 26 financial assistance for` `claim: primary victim, every cap reached`)'s `for actual loss of earnings` EQUALS 20000
#ASSERT (`the s 26 financial assistance for` `claim: primary victim, every cap reached`)'s `for out-of-pocket expenses` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`the s 26 financial assistance for` `claim: primary victim, every cap reached`)'s `for medical and dental expenses` EQUALS 9000
#ASSERT (`the s 26 financial assistance for` `claim: primary victim, every cap reached`)'s `for justice related expenses` EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT (`the s 26 financial assistance for` `claim: primary victim, every cap reached`)'s `for clothing and personal effects` EQUALS 500
#ASSERT (`the s 26 financial assistance for` `claim: primary victim, every cap reached`)'s `for economic loss, within the maximum` EQUALS 30000
#ASSERT (`the s 26 financial assistance for` `claim: primary victim, every cap reached`)'s `taken off under s 26(2) or s 27(2)` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`the s 26 financial assistance for` `claim: primary victim, every cap reached`)'s `in total` EQUALS 35000

`claim: primary victim, no earnings shown` MEANS
    `Primary victim claim` WITH
        `immediate needs expenses`                                           IS (`Expense` WITH `amount` IS 0, `paid or payable from another source` IS 0)
        `can demonstrate actual loss of earnings`                            IS FALSE
        `weekly rate of actual loss of earnings under cl 9`                  IS 800
        `weeks of actual loss of earnings`                                   IS 5
        `lost earnings paid or payable from another source`                  IS 0
        `out-of-pocket expenses`                                             IS (`Expense` WITH `amount` IS 6500, `paid or payable from another source` IS 500)
        `medical and dental expenses not claimed as immediate needs`         IS (`Expense` WITH `amount` IS 0, `paid or payable from another source` IS 0)
        `justice related expenses`                                           IS (`Expense` WITH `amount` IS 0, `paid or payable from another source` IS 0)
        `clothing and personal effects`                                      IS (`Expense` WITH `amount` IS 0, `paid or payable from another source` IS 0)
        `paid or approved to the parent, step-parent or guardian under s 27` IS 0

-- no actual loss of earnings shown: earnings 0 (the rate is not used); out-of-pocket 6,500 - 500 = 6,000, capped at 5,000; total 5,000
#ASSERT (`the s 26 financial assistance for` `claim: primary victim, no earnings shown`)'s `for immediate needs` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`the s 26 financial assistance for` `claim: primary victim, no earnings shown`)'s `for actual loss of earnings` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`the s 26 financial assistance for` `claim: primary victim, no earnings shown`)'s `for out-of-pocket expenses` EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT (`the s 26 financial assistance for` `claim: primary victim, no earnings shown`)'s `for medical and dental expenses` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`the s 26 financial assistance for` `claim: primary victim, no earnings shown`)'s `for justice related expenses` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`the s 26 financial assistance for` `claim: primary victim, no earnings shown`)'s `for clothing and personal effects` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`the s 26 financial assistance for` `claim: primary victim, no earnings shown`)'s `for economic loss, within the maximum` EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT (`the s 26 financial assistance for` `claim: primary victim, no earnings shown`)'s `taken off under s 26(2) or s 27(2)` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`the s 26 financial assistance for` `claim: primary victim, no earnings shown`)'s `in total` EQUALS 5000

