§§ `s 36, s 53, Reg cl 14 -- recognition payments`

-- s 36(1)(a)(i), cl 14(a) $15,000
#ASSERT `the recognition payments for` `facts: a homicide` `to` `recipient: a financially dependent spouse` EQUALS (LIST (`a recognition payment` `category A (s 35(1))` 15000))
-- s 36(1)(b)(ii), cl 14(b) $7,500
#ASSERT `the recognition payments for` `facts: a homicide` `to` `recipient: a spouse, not dependent` EQUALS (LIST (`a recognition payment` `category A (s 35(1))` 7500))
-- s 36(1)(b)(ii) needs the s 22(3)(b) 2 years
#ASSERT `the recognition payments for` `facts: a homicide` `to` `recipient: a de facto partner of 18 months` EQUALS (LIST (`no recognition payment` `the act is category A, which s 36(1)(a) and (b) pay only to listed members of the family of the primary victim who died`))
-- not a family victim (s 22(3)(b)), so not s 36(1)(a)(i) either
#ASSERT `the recognition payments for` `facts: a homicide` `to` `recipient: a dependent de facto partner of 18 months` EQUALS (LIST (`no recognition payment` `the act is category A, which s 36(1)(a) and (b) pay only to listed members of the family of the primary victim who died`))
-- s 36(1)(a)(ii)
#ASSERT `the recognition payments for` `facts: a homicide` `to` `recipient: a child aged 12` EQUALS (LIST (`a recognition payment` `category A (s 35(1))` 15000))
-- s 36(1)(a)(ii) only under 18; (b) lists only parents and partners (finding 14)
#ASSERT `the recognition payments for` `facts: a homicide` `to` `recipient: an adult child, not dependent` EQUALS (LIST (`no recognition payment` `the act is category A, which s 36(1)(a) and (b) pay only to listed members of the family of the primary victim who died`))
-- s 36(1)(a)(i)
#ASSERT `the recognition payments for` `facts: a homicide` `to` `recipient: an adult child, dependent` EQUALS (LIST (`a recognition payment` `category A (s 35(1))` 15000))
-- s 36(1)(b)(i)
#ASSERT `the recognition payments for` `facts: a homicide` `to` `recipient: a parent, not dependent` EQUALS (LIST (`a recognition payment` `category A (s 35(1))` 7500))
-- a sibling must be dependent (finding 14)
#ASSERT `the recognition payments for` `facts: a homicide` `to` `recipient: a brother, not dependent` EQUALS (LIST (`no recognition payment` `the act is category A, which s 36(1)(a) and (b) pay only to listed members of the family of the primary victim who died`))
-- s 36(1)(a)(i)
#ASSERT `the recognition payments for` `facts: a homicide` `to` `recipient: a brother, dependent` EQUALS (LIST (`a recognition payment` `category A (s 35(1))` 15000))
-- s 36(1)(a)(ii) says "child", not step-child (finding 14)
#ASSERT `the recognition payments for` `facts: a homicide` `to` `recipient: a step-child aged 12, not dependent` EQUALS (LIST (`no recognition payment` `the act is category A, which s 36(1)(a) and (b) pay only to listed members of the family of the primary victim who died`))
-- s 29(3), (4)(b) read with s 36(1)(a) (READING, finding 14)
#ASSERT `the recognition payments for` `facts: a homicide` `to` `recipient: a child born after the death` EQUALS (LIST (`a recognition payment` `category A (s 35(1))` 15000))
-- category A is never paid to a primary victim
#ASSERT `the recognition payments for` `facts: a homicide` `to` `recipient: an injured primary victim` EQUALS (LIST (`no recognition payment` `the act is category A, which s 36(1)(a) and (b) pay only to listed members of the family of the primary victim who died`))
-- B and C describe it; the higher, B, cl 14(c) $10,000
#ASSERT `the recognition payments for` `facts: a sexual assault with a weapon` `to` `recipient: an injured primary victim` EQUALS (LIST (`a recognition payment` `category B (s 35(2))` 10000))
-- cl 14(d) $5,000
#ASSERT `the recognition payments for` `facts: a sexual assault` `to` `recipient: an injured primary victim` EQUALS (LIST (`a recognition payment` `category C (s 35(3))` 5000))
-- cl 14(c)
#ASSERT `the recognition payments for` `facts: sexual assaults in a series` `to` `recipient: an injured primary victim` EQUALS (LIST (`a recognition payment` `category B (s 35(2))` 10000))
-- cl 14(e) $1,500
#ASSERT `the recognition payments for` `facts: sexual touching` `to` `recipient: an injured primary victim` EQUALS (LIST (`a recognition payment` `category D (s 35(4))` 1500))
-- B over D
#ASSERT `the recognition payments for` `facts: sexual touching in a series` `to` `recipient: an injured primary victim` EQUALS (LIST (`a recognition payment` `category B (s 35(2))` 10000))
-- C
#ASSERT `the recognition payments for` `facts: a violent attempted sexual assault causing serious bodily injury` `to` `recipient: an injured primary victim` EQUALS (LIST (`a recognition payment` `category C (s 35(3))` 5000))
-- C over D
#ASSERT `the recognition payments for` `facts: physical assaults of a child in a series` `to` `recipient: an injured primary victim` EQUALS (LIST (`a recognition payment` `category C (s 35(3))` 5000))
-- D
#ASSERT `the recognition payments for` `facts: a physical assault of a child` `to` `recipient: an injured primary victim` EQUALS (LIST (`a recognition payment` `category D (s 35(4))` 1500))
-- C
#ASSERT `the recognition payments for` `facts: an assault causing grievous bodily harm` `to` `recipient: an injured primary victim` EQUALS (LIST (`a recognition payment` `category C (s 35(3))` 5000))
-- D
#ASSERT `the recognition payments for` `facts: a violent robbery` `to` `recipient: an injured primary victim` EQUALS (LIST (`a recognition payment` `category D (s 35(4))` 1500))
-- no s 35 category
#ASSERT `the recognition payments for` `facts: none of the kinds` `to` `recipient: an injured primary victim` EQUALS (LIST (`no recognition payment` `no category in s 35 describes the act`))
-- D is payable only to an injured primary victim
#ASSERT `the recognition payments for` `facts: an assault` `to` `recipient: a financially dependent spouse` EQUALS (LIST (`no recognition payment` `categories B, C and D are payable only to a primary victim who suffered injury (s 36(1)(c) to (e))`))
-- s 36(2)
#ASSERT `the recognition payments for` `facts: an assault` `to` `recipient: an injured primary victim, already paid for the series` EQUALS (LIST (`no recognition payment` `only one recognition payment is payable for a series of related acts against the victim (s 36(2))`))
-- s 19(6): not related to the earlier act
#ASSERT `the recognition payments for` `facts: an assault` `to` `recipient: an injured primary victim, a later act after support` EQUALS (LIST (`a recognition payment` `category D (s 35(4))` 1500))
-- s 53
#ASSERT `the recognition payments for` `facts: an assault` `to` `recipient: an injured primary victim, review pending` EQUALS (LIST (`a recognition payment, suspended pending the Tribunal's review (s 53)` `category D (s 35(4))` 1500))
-- s 53: "Subject to any order of the Tribunal to the contrary"
#ASSERT `the recognition payments for` `facts: an assault` `to` `recipient: an injured primary victim, review pending, Tribunal orders payment` EQUALS (LIST (`a recognition payment` `category D (s 35(4))` 1500))
-- both: category A as spouse (s 36(1)(b)) and D as an injured primary victim (finding 13)
#ASSERT `the recognition payments for` `facts: a homicide by an assault` `to` `recipient: an injured spouse, not dependent` EQUALS (LIST (`a recognition payment` `category A (s 35(1))` 7500), (`a recognition payment` `category D (s 35(4))` 1500))
-- s 53
#ASSERT `the recognition payments for` `facts: a homicide` `to` `recipient: a financially dependent spouse, review pending` EQUALS (LIST (`a recognition payment, suspended pending the Tribunal's review (s 53)` `category A (s 35(1))` 15000))

§§ `Reg cl 5, 7 -- counselling hours`

`counselling: a primary victim, none used` MEANS
    `Counselling facts` WITH
        `counselling class`                                                       IS `a primary or secondary victim`
        `whether the person is a victim is still being established`               IS FALSE
        `the counselling is provided outside Australia`                           IS FALSE
        `the counsellor's hourly fee outside Australia`                           IS 0
        `is, or was while under 18, a victim of sexual assault or physical abuse` IS FALSE
        `hours of counselling already paid for the act`                           IS 0

-- cl 5(2): 22 hours
#ASSERT `the counselling hours for` `counselling: a primary victim, none used` EQUALS (`up to this many more hours, and further periods if the Commissioner considers it appropriate; more than 22 hours in all only for exceptional reasons (cl 5(2), (4))` 22)

