        `kind of support`                                                                          IS `funeral expenses`
        `the victim's date of birth`                                                               IS (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1970)
        `the day the act occurred`                                                                 IS (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2019)
        `is a family victim, and the cause of death was only established later`                    IS FALSE
        `the day it was established that the death was a direct result of the act`                 IS (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2024)
        `the act involved domestic violence, child abuse or sexual assault`                        IS FALSE
        `is a primary victim of an act of violence in the course of a sexual offence against them` IS FALSE

-- s 40(2) does not apply
#ASSERT `the time limit for` `timing: an adult, a date established given but not later established` EQUALS (`apply on or before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2021) `s 40(1): 2 years after the act`)

`timing: an adult, act on 29 February` MEANS
    `Application timing` WITH
        `kind of support`                                                                          IS `financial assistance for immediate needs`
        `the victim's date of birth`                                                               IS (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1990)
        `the day the act occurred`                                                                 IS (DATE_FROM_DMY 29 2 2024)
        `is a family victim, and the cause of death was only established later`                    IS FALSE
        `the day it was established that the death was a direct result of the act`                 IS (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000)
        `the act involved domestic violence, child abuse or sexual assault`                        IS FALSE
        `is a primary victim of an act of violence in the course of a sexual offence against them` IS FALSE

-- READING: 28 February 2026
#ASSERT `the time limit for` `timing: an adult, act on 29 February` EQUALS (`apply on or before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 2026) `s 40(1): 2 years after the act`)

`timing: a child the day before turning 18` MEANS
    `Application timing` WITH
        `kind of support`                                                                          IS `financial assistance for immediate needs`
        `the victim's date of birth`                                                               IS (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 3 2007)
        `the day the act occurred`                                                                 IS (DATE_FROM_DMY 9 3 2025)
        `is a family victim, and the cause of death was only established later`                    IS FALSE
        `the day it was established that the death was a direct result of the act`                 IS (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000)
        `the act involved domestic violence, child abuse or sexual assault`                        IS FALSE
        `is a primary victim of an act of violence in the course of a sexual offence against them` IS FALSE

-- a child on 9 March 2025: 18 on 10 March 2025, + 2 years
#ASSERT `the time limit for` `timing: a child the day before turning 18` EQUALS (`apply on or before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 3 2027) `s 40(1): 2 years after the victim turns 18`)

-- In time: on the last day, yes; the day after, no. No time limit: always.
#ASSERT `an application made on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 3 2025) `is in time for` `timing: an adult, immediate needs`
#ASSERT NOT (`an application made on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 11 3 2025) `is in time for` `timing: an adult, immediate needs`)
#ASSERT `an application made on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2060) `is in time for` `timing: a child sexual offence victim, recognition`
#ASSERT `an application made on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2026) `is in time for` `timing: a family victim, cause of death established later, funeral`
#ASSERT NOT (`an application made on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 9 2026) `is in time for` `timing: a family victim, cause of death established later, funeral`)
-- The days for the regulative rule: 10 March 2023 to 10 March 2025 is 731 days; none where there is no limit.
#ASSERT `the days from the act to the last day to apply for` `timing: an adult, immediate needs` EQUALS JUST 731
#ASSERT `the days from the act to the last day to apply for` `timing: a child sexual offence victim, recognition` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 40(6): an application made 1 July 2023 takes claims up to and including 1 July 2028.
#ASSERT `whether claims may be made under an application made on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2023) `on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2028) `when` FALSE EQUALS `claims may be made under the application up to and including` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2028)
#ASSERT `whether claims may be made under an application made on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2023) `on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 7 2028) `when` FALSE EQUALS `no further claims: 5 years have passed since the application was made (s 40(6)(a))`
#ASSERT `whether claims may be made under an application made on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2023) `on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 8 2024) `when` TRUE EQUALS `no further claims: the total maximum amount of financial support has been given (s 40(6)(b))`

§§ `Regulative rules -- traces`

-- s 40(1), 731 days: applied on day 400, determined on day 500.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 40 -- the application must be duly made in time` (JUST 731)) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `duly make the application for financial support or a recognition payment` 400), (EVENT `the Commissioner` `determine the application and give the applicant written notice` 500)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Applied on the last day, day 731: in time.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 40 -- the application must be duly made in time` (JUST 731)) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `duly make the application for financial support or a recognition payment` 731), (EVENT `the Commissioner` `determine the application and give the applicant written notice` 800)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- s 40(7), no time limit: applied after 25 years.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 40 -- the application must be duly made in time` NOTHING) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `duly make the application for financial support or a recognition payment` 9200), (EVENT `the Commissioner` `determine the application and give the applicant written notice` 9300)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the applicant, "s 40: the application ... was not duly made within the time allowed ..." (applied on day 732)
#TRACE `s 40 -- the application must be duly made in time` (JUST 731) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the applicant` DOES `duly make the application for financial support or a recognition payment` AT 732

-- expect: BREACH BY the applicant, "s 40: ..." (no application; day 800 passes)
#TRACE `s 40 -- the application must be duly made in time` (JUST 731) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 800)

-- expect: the s 43 obligation still pending: PARTY the Commissioner MUST determine ... (no period is stated)
#TRACE `s 40 -- the application must be duly made in time` (JUST 731) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the applicant` DOES `duly make the application for financial support or a recognition payment` AT 100
    (WAITUNTIL 5000)

-- s 40(6), application made 1 July 2023: 1827 days to 1 July 2028. Claim on day 1000, paid on day 1010.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 40(6) -- claims under a duly made application, for 5 years or until the maximum is given` 1827 FALSE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `make a claim under the application` 1000), (EVENT `the Commissioner` `pay the amount claimed, subject to the conditions of the approval` 1010)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Claim on the last day, day 1827.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 40(6) -- claims under a duly made application, for 5 years or until the maximum is given` 1827 FALSE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `make a claim under the application` 1827), (EVENT `the Commissioner` `pay the amount claimed, subject to the conditions of the approval` 1830)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the applicant, "s 40(6)(a): 5 years have passed ..." (the period ends; a claim on day 1900)
#TRACE `s 40(6) -- claims under a duly made application, for 5 years or until the maximum is given` 1827 FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 1828)
    PARTY `the applicant` DOES `make a claim under the application` AT 1900

-- expect: BREACH BY the applicant, "s 40(6)(b): the total maximum ... has been given ..." (a claim on day 10)
#TRACE `s 40(6) -- claims under a duly made application, for 5 years or until the maximum is given` 1827 TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the applicant` DOES `make a claim under the application` AT 10

-- expect: the s 54(2) obligation still pending: PARTY the Commissioner MUST pay ... (claimed on day 50, not yet paid)
#TRACE `s 40(6) -- claims under a duly made application, for 5 years or until the maximum is given` 1827 FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the applicant` DOES `make a claim under the application` AT 50

